 "notes": "Linear spine with one hub: dispersion (c12) is the structural claim every property branch uses (crystallinity, thermal, UV). Image audits change the argument: (1) F7 TEM shows clustered TiO2 in every panel, contradicting 'very good dispersion' (c14 contradicts); the hub claim therefore rests on SEM at magnifications that cannot resolve 40-70 nm particles (c13 partial). (2) F11a: the 5-20 wt% transmittance curves coincide, contradicting the loading trend, and composites attenuate strongly across 400-550 nm (c28 text-silent), which qualifies the 'UV-selective, transparent' performance claim; the photograph (c29) shows readable but hazy films. (3) Char yield rise is arithmetic filler residue (c20), qualifying the thermal-stability claim; only T5/T10 carry it. c17: crystallinity reduction read from stacked a.u. traces is weak. F8 AFM (topography, particle ~70 nm) folded into c15 attrs rather than a node. PRC c7 ultrasonic mixing + casting typed forming (composite mixing-and-solidification), could also be deposition if films were cast on a substrate; packet says films were cast and dried, not coated.",
 "migrated_from": "r03/graphs/Progress_in_Organic_Coatings__j.porgcoat.2011.04.010.json"
}